        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: load plan utilization history off the startup main thread",
        "body": "## Problem\n\n`UsageStore.init` previously called `PlanUtilizationHistoryStore.load()` synchronously on the main actor. A mature two-year, two-provider history blocks the startup main thread for ~150 ms (Release benchmark from the original audit).\n\n## Fix\n\nMove the decode onto a utility-priority detached task and publish the result through the existing `planUtilizationHistoryRevision` path:\n\n- `PlanUtilizationHistoryStore` and its cross-task types are now `Sendable`; the store gains a `loadAsync()` helper.\n- `UsageStore.init` starts a one-shot background load task. In-memory history starts empty.\n- A new `planUtilizationHistoryLoaded` flag gates sync menu accessors and mutation paths so a startup refresh cannot overwrite real disk history with an empty in-memory stub.\n- `recordPlanUtilizationHistorySample` awaits the load before mutating.\n\nThe load publishes exactly once via a generation-guarded write.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New `UsageStorePlanUtilizationAsyncLoadTests` covers the gate-released publish path, sync menu gating, empty/corrupt file best-effort, multi-provider/multi-account ownership preservation, and init independence from history size.\n- Existing `UsageStorePlanUtilizationTests.makeStore` and `UsageStorePlanUtilizationClaudeIdentityTests.makeReloadedStoreWithConfiguredTokenAccount` updated to cancel/await the load via new test seams (`_cancelPlanUtilizationHistoryLoadForTesting`, `_waitForPlanUtilizationHistoryLoadForTesting`) to preserve their pre-async-load intent.\n- One `StatusMenuHighlightTests` flake (`hosted submenu close resumes deferred explicit rebuild on fresh parent`) was caused by the load's revision bump landing inside the test's yield loop; the test now cancels the load deterministically.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `swift test --filter PlanUtilization`: 144/144 pass\n- `swift test --filter StatusMenu`: 349/349 pass\n- `swift test --filter StatusMenuHostedSubmenuRefreshTests`: 11/11 pass\n- `swift test --filter UsageStoreDisabledProviderCleanupTests`: 4/4 pass (from #3)\n- `swift test --filter AgentSessionMenuDescriptorTests`: 8/8 pass (from #1)\n- `make check`: 0 violations\n\n`KiroStatusProbeTests.accepted pipe output cannot overrun the usage deadline` is a pre-existing flake unrelated to this PR — it fails under `make test` parallel-group scheduling but passes in isolation, and its assertions about PTY marker file cleanup touch no code paths this PR modifies.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nJSON schema, two-year retention policy, account ownership and ordering semantics are unchanged. This does not change the persistence format, sampling frequency, chart rendering, or Cost History. It only moves the existing on-disk decode off the startup critical path.",
